MID_SC13_00_m01: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m01_001: Troy's directions put Mahadu's shrine just ahead...
MID_SC13_00_m16: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m01_002: You should not have come here, woman. It will be\na fatal mistake.
MID_SC13_00_m01_003: You are a Har Hali, I take it. Then you have common\ncause with the man who maimed me.
MID_SC13_00_m01_004: Is he here as well, watching from the shadows?
MID_SC13_00_m01_005: No matter. I cannot withdraw, and so I must force\nmy way through with all my strength!
MID_SC13_00_m02: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m02_001: I must eliminate those who stand in the way of\n{SetColor=Gold}Mahadu's shrine{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC13_00_m02_002: Though one warrior, with one arm, may not be\nenough...
MID_SC13_00_m03: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m03_001: It is you... I will see you dead on this ground.
MID_SC13_00_m03_002: I can feel him here. No doubt remains in my mind\nthat he is watching from somewhere.
MID_SC13_00_m03_003: The man who stole my arm...
MID_SC13_00_m04: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m04_001: Ngh... The Har Hali are formidable indeed. I won't\ncut through them like this...
MID_SC13_00_m13: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m04_002: That's what we're here for, boss!
MID_SC13_00_m04_003: Tobias! Bonaventure! Why have you come?!
MID_SC13_00_m04_004: Nothing could keep us away. We shall always be\nyour attendants through thick and thin.
MID_SC13_00_m04_005: Whatever you say, boss, we'll do! We'll be your arms\nfor you!
MID_SC13_00_m04_006: Brave warriors...thank you. To arms! I must break\nthrough to what waits beyond!
MID_SC13_00_m04_007: If that's what you want, that's what you'll get!
MID_SC13_00_m12: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m12_001: You're a hard one to chase after.
MID_SC13_00_m12_002: Why'd you go and leave us behind?!
MID_SC13_00_m12_003: Tobias! Bonaventure! Why have you come?!
MID_SC13_00_m12_004: Nothing could keep us away. We shall always be\nyour attendants through thick and thin.
MID_SC13_00_m12_005: Whatever you say, boss, we'll do! We'll be your arms\nfor you!
MID_SC13_00_m12_006: Brave warriors...thank you. To arms! I must break\nthrough to what waits beyond!
MID_SC13_00_m12_007: If that's what you want, that's what you'll get!
MID_SC13_00_m06: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m06_001: Now's your chance, boss! Into Mahadu's shrine\nyou go!
MID_SC13_00_m06_002: You have my thanks. Both of you.
MID_SC13_00_m06_003: Hold those thanks until the deed is done. Quickly,\nwhile we keep them at bay!
MID_SC13_00_m14: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m06_004: Hm? Has the time come to spring our trap?\nThat shrine will be her tomb.
MID_SC13_00_m15: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m06_005: What did he say?! My lady, be careful!
MID_SC13_00_m07: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m07_001: I don't believe it. The arm snapped right on!\nWhat in the world happened in there, boss?
MID_SC13_00_m07_002: It was Mahadu. He granted the power held in his\narm to me.
MID_SC13_00_m07_003: It's incredible. One Mahadu arm on our side is\nworth one hundred troops!
MID_SC13_00_m08: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m08_001: I can't believe my eyes. To see you bearing the arm\nof a two-hundred-year-old corpse...
MID_SC13_00_m08_002: And yet it moves as if I had been born with it.\nIt is a gift I shall not decline.
MID_SC13_00_m08_003: Quite. To see it flex in battle...I can see no other\nexplanation than that you are favored by Mahadu.
MID_SC13_00_m09: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m09_001: That arm changes nothing. You remain fated to\ndie here...
MID_SC13_00_m10: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m10_001: Only death awaits those who stand against me.
MID_SC13_00_m11: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_m11_001: Mahadu. I am grateful for this blessing of power.
MID_SC13_00_e01: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_e01_001: I may not be able to fight at my usual standard.
MID_SC13_00_e02: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_e02_001: The {SetColor=Gold}brush{SetColor=Default} should afford me some small {SetColor=Gold}advantage{SetColor=Default}.\nIf I'm in there, I can even the odds.
MID_SC13_00_e08: <TH>
MID_SC13_00_e08_001: This strength I feel is unlike any I have ever known.\nSo this is Mahadu's power...
MID_SC13_01_m01: <TH>
MID_SC13_01_m01_001: Stow your sword, Commander. Why would a loyal\nretainer side with Dyan?
MID_SC13_01_m01_002: Does it matter? I have thrown in my lot with\nPrince Dyan. I cannot revoke that choice.
MID_SC13_01_m01_003: Does the favor you received from King Sergio\nmean nothing to you?!
MID_SC13_01_m01_004: My path is set, Commander Bonaventure. I will not\nturn from it now.
MID_SC13_01_m01_005: Gah! You obstinate old fool!
MID_SC13_01_m02: <TH>
MID_SC13_01_m02_001: Princess Theodora! As a commander sworn to\nPrince Dyan, I will take your life!
MID_SC13_01_m02_002: Never let it be said you are disloyal, Commander\nHuver. Now back those words up with action!
MID_SC13_01_m03: <TH>
MID_SC13_01_m03_001: I have made my choice. If this is where it leads,\nthen so be it!
MID_SC13_01_m04: <TH>
MID_SC13_01_m04_001: I don't know where you got that arm...but I will show\nyou my fitness to rule!
MID_SC13_01_m04_002: I am stronger than you, my dear sister! I alone\ndeserve the throne!
MID_SC13_01_m05: <TH>
MID_SC13_01_m05_001: Can't you cretins see that this is my moment?!\nPerhaps you need convincing!
MID_SC13_01_e02: <TH>
MID_SC13_01_e02_001: Magic courses through {SetColor=Gold}those tiles{SetColor=Default}. Position yourself\nthere and you will {SetColor=Gold}more easily evade enemy attacks{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC13_01_e03: <TH>
MID_SC13_01_e03_001: Huver! Show my dear sister she came here to die!
MID_SC13_01_e04: <TH>
MID_SC13_01_e04_001: As...as you command, Prince Dyan.
MID_SC13_01_e06: <TH>
MID_SC13_01_e06_001: Huver has fallen already?! Damn him. Where was\nhis vaunted strength when I needed it?
MID_SC13_01_e06_002: You will soon follow, Dyan. Let us make an end of\nthis futile exercise.
MID_SC13_01_e07: <TH>
MID_SC13_01_e07_001: What are you standing around for? Kill her!\nKill her NOW!
MID_SC13_02_m01: <TH>
MID_SC13_02_m01_001: What happened here, Your Majesty? Actually,\nI think I see it clearly enough.
MID_SC13_02_m01_002: Heh! Never a dull moment in the big city, am I right?
MID_SC13_02_m01_003: You are just in time to punish the scoundrels who\ndared break into this temple.
MID_SC13_02_m02: <TH>
MID_SC13_02_m02_001: So this is where you've been, priest lady. We were\nlooking all over!
MID_SC13_02_m02_002: Wait, how did you get yourself into another fight?!\nWe really can't take you anywhere.
MID_SC13_02_m02_003: OK, don't worry. We're here to help!
MID_SC13_02_m02_004: Heh. Look at you, starting to stand your ground.
MID_SC13_02_m03: <TH>
MID_SC13_02_m03_001: Um, try not to damage the temple if you can!
MID_SC13_02_m03_002: Yu Phas may no longer be with us, but this is still\nsacred ground.
MID_SC13_02_m03_003: True enough. My apologies. I'll take greater care\nhenceforth.
MID_SC13_02_m03_004: She doesn't seem too surprised at the boss's strength.
MID_SC13_02_m03_005: Yes... There's something strange about her, even\nbeyond the obvious.
MID_SC13_02_m04: <TH>
MID_SC13_02_m04_001: Who are these people? What have we gotten\nourselves into?!
MID_SC13_02_m05: <TH>
MID_SC13_02_m05_001: I cannot abide scoundrels plundering a temple—\neven an abandoned one.
MID_SC13_02_m06: <TH>
MID_SC13_02_m06_001: Damn it! This was supposed to be an easy job!
MID_SC13_02_e02: <TH>
MID_SC13_02_e02_001: What the— These folks are way too strong! Of course\nthey'd be the ones to stumble across our little heist...
MID_SC13_02_e02_002: Hey! You've still {SetColor=Gold}got the bullion{SetColor=Default} we stole, right?\nHide, so they can't take it from you!
MID_SC13_02_e04: <TH>
MID_SC13_02_e04_001: Will do! I'll stay tucked away right here.
MID_SC13_02_e04_002: Setting up for an ambush, I see. My Earthen Throw\nattack ought to put paid to that.
MID_SC13_04_m01: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_m01_001: Rrrghhh...
MID_SC13_04_m01_002: Our foe is even more disturbing than I'd heard.
MID_SC13_04_m01_003: Let's just focus on the fight. We can't spend the\nmatch complaining.
MID_SC13_04_m01_004: That's how easy wins turn into losses, you see.\nI'd rather avoid that.
MID_SC13_04_m01_005: I fear that less than I fear you holding us back.
MID_SC13_04_m02: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_m02_001: I must say... Your reputation may precede you, but\nit does not do you justice.
MID_SC13_04_m02_002: Even so, I can tell much of your strength is drawn\nfrom that arm of yours. Isn't that right?
MID_SC13_04_m02_003: We don't need to discuss the details now, of course.\nThat can wait until after we win.
MID_SC13_04_m02_004: This Talimun of Vandahl Trading is perceptive.
MID_SC13_04_m02_005: I would sooner not make an enemy of him without\nknowing his true intentions.
MID_SC13_04_m03: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_m03_001: What in the world?! Bonaventure, did you see that?
MID_SC13_04_m03_002: It looked like some sort of sorcery, but none I have\never encountered.
MID_SC13_04_m03_003: I've heard tell of such things before but never seen\nthe genuine article.
MID_SC13_04_m03_004: Among the tools our ancestors used were small,\ncylindrical devices that spat fire.
MID_SC13_04_m03_005: Then they may indeed be People of the White Egg?
MID_SC13_04_m04: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_m04_001: Now, that's an intriguing device. Doesn't appear to\ntake gunpowder either.
MID_SC13_04_m04_002: It must use some sort of magic. Something created by\nthe mages of Morfis, perhaps.
MID_SC13_04_m04_003: Perhaps... You know, I was just taking a shot in the\ndark before, but might have hit the nail on the head.
MID_SC13_04_m04_004: My warmest welcome to the People of the White\nEgg! I'll need to ask about that later...
MID_SC13_04_m05: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_m05_001: You...the woman from that day. I have not forgotten.
MID_SC13_04_m05_002: A throng of people desire revenge on me. You do\nnot stand out especially.
MID_SC13_04_m06: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_m06_001: Hnk... Oogh... I will send you all to the underworld...
MID_SC13_04_m07: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_m07_001: Graah!
MID_SC13_04_m07_002: This guy gives me the creeps. I think I'll be keeping\nmy distance...
MID_SC13_04_m07_003: Very well. Then I'll dispatch him myself.
MID_SC13_04_e02: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_e02_002: Those {SetColor=Gold}ballistae{SetColor=Default} will be troublesome. It would be\nunwise to advance without accounting for them.
MID_SC13_04_e02_003: Yeah, I know. If only our options weren't so slim...
MID_SC13_04_e03: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_e03_001: Wait, do you feel that? The breeze, and the moisture\nin the air... {SetColor=Gold}It's going to rain soon!{SetColor=Default}
MID_SC13_04_e03_002: They probably {SetColor=Gold}can't use their ballistae {SetColor=Default}while it's\nraining. Everyone, that'll be our opening!
MID_SC13_04_e04: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_e04_001: The {SetColor=Gold}rain will start{SetColor=Default} any minute now. Let's make sure\nwe're ready to capitalize on it.
MID_SC13_04_e05: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_e05_001: Damn, the{SetColor=Gold} rain's about to stop{SetColor=Default}. Alright, then,\nfinal push!
MID_SC13_04_e10: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_e10_001: <DLG>It will start raining on the next turn.
MID_SC13_04_e11: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_e11_001: <DLG>It will stop raining on the next turn.
MID_SC13_04_e06: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_e06_001: <DLG>It has started raining. Ballistae cannot be used.
MID_SC13_04_e07: <TH>
MID_SC13_04_e07_001: <DLG>It has stopped raining. Ballistae can now be used.
MID_BD13_04_m01: <TH>
MID_BD13_04_m01_001: You know this guy, Majesty? You should have\nsaid something.
MID_BD13_04_m01_002: Though it looks like maybe you're not on the best\nof terms, eh?
MID_BD13_04_m01_003: Enough with your jesting. Our enemy is\ndeadly serious.
MID_BD13_04_m05: <TH>
MID_BD13_04_m01_004: What was that sound?
MID_BD13_04_m06: <TH>
MID_BD13_04_m01_005: The chain Troy gave me... It's cracked?
MID_BD13_04_m07: <TH>
MID_BD13_04_m01_006: But I warn you, Theodora. The warding chain will\nabsorb the arm's malice only up to a point.
MID_BD13_04_m01_007: If you see it begin to crack, it is straining against\nits limits. That may mean the end of you.
MID_BD13_04_m08: <TH>
MID_BD13_04_m01_008: Damn it!
MID_BD13_04_m02: <TH>
MID_BD13_04_m02_001: Impressive...but I didn't come this far to lose.
MID_BD13_04_m02_002: I may as well try that flamma they gave me before\nthe match...
MID_BD13_04_m09: <TH>
MID_BD13_04_m02_003: Rrgh!
MID_BD13_04_m10: <TH>
MID_BD13_04_m02_004: Oogh... AAAAAAGH!
MID_BD13_04_m11: <TH>
MID_BD13_04_m02_005: He seems...different now...
MID_BD13_04_m02_006: What was that he drank? It didn't look like one of\nthe Har Hali's secret elixirs.
MID_BD13_04_m02_007: Shameless. Anyone who would so brazenly violate\nthe spirit of the competition must face punishment!
MID_BD13_04_m03: <TH>
MID_BD13_04_m03_001: I will send all before me...to their graves... To the\ndarkness of Balor, beyond the void of night...
MID_BD13_04_m04: <TH>
MID_BD13_04_m04_001: Haaagh... Haaagh...
MID_BD13_04_m04_002: He was tough, but we brought him down.
MID_BD13_04_e01: <TH>
MID_BD13_04_e01_001: There we have it!
MID_BD13_04_e01_002: Emerging triumphant after a glorious battle...
MID_BD13_04_e02: <TH>
MID_BD13_04_e01_003: The mighty fighters of the Eastern Division!
MID_BD13_04_e01_004: Citizens, give a round of applause!
MID_BD13_05_m01: <TH>
MID_BD13_05_m01_001: While you remain free, you haunt my nightmares.
MID_BD13_05_m03: <TH>
MID_BD13_05_m01_002: I will count robbing me of my sleep among your\nmany sins.
MID_BD13_05_m02: <TH>
MID_BD13_05_m02_001: Hgh... Your arm...belongs to me... You will return\nit to me...
MID_BD13_05_m04: <TH>
MID_BD13_05_m02_002: What an odd thing to say.
MID_BD13_05_m02_003: I was blessed with this arm directly by Mahadu,\na hero of the Saraminian people.
MID_BD13_05_m05: <TH>
MID_BD13_05_m02_004: You have no claim to it that I can see.
MID_SC13_06_m01: <TH>
MID_SC13_06_m01_001: Hahaha! This is fun, White-Maned Demon! You are\na truer warrior than I thought!
MID_SC13_06_m01_002: Thanks...I suppose. You're not half bad yourself.
MID_SC13_06_m02: <TH>
MID_SC13_06_m02_001: Your axe style is unique but beautiful.\nVery thorough—you leave no openings.
MID_SC13_06_m02_002: I know not who taught you, but they must have\nbeen a legend in their own right.
MID_SC13_06_m03: <TH>
MID_SC13_06_m03_001: He does not lack for a killer's resolve. He's simply\na more honest soul than I thought.
MID_SC13_06_m03_002: Hehe. How long has it been since I sparred with\nsuch a man?
MID_SC13_06_m04: <TH>
MID_SC13_06_m04_001: I am not done fighting.
MID_SC13_06_m04_002: Interesting. I sense power from that man's axe.
MID_SC13_06_m04_003: There is a red glow from between the cracks on\nits surface.
MID_SC13_06_m04_004: And it feels as if it's in harmony with my arm...
MID_SC13_06_m04_005: Could this be another of Drake's treasures?
MID_SC13_06_e01: <TH>
MID_SC13_06_e01_001: <DLG>Bertrand used Flash Awakening. His physical protection\nwill be increased until his next phase.
MID_SC13_06_e02: <TH>
MID_SC13_06_e02_001: <DLG>Bertrand used Storm Awakening. He has greater ability to dodge\nattacks until his next phase.
MID_SC13_06_e03: <TH>
MID_SC13_06_e03_001: <DLG>Bertrand used Ruler's Awakening. His accuracy will be increased\nuntil his next phase.
MID_SC13_06_e04: <TH>
MID_SC13_06_e04_001: I have taken your measure in combat, White-Maned\nDemon, and I am impressed.
MID_SC13_07_m01: <TH>
MID_SC13_07_m01_001: How dare that accursed man defile the temple of\nYu Phas with his presence.
MID_SC13_07_m01_002: He will not leave here alive. He, and any others of\nhis ilk, cannot go unchecked.
MID_SC13_07_m02: <TH>
MID_SC13_07_m02_001: Damn him! What unnatural power is this?
MID_SC13_07_m02_002: That liquid he drank seemed the same as what\nhe used in our last encounter.
MID_SC13_07_m02_003: Hong Hua, what do you know of this?
MID_SC13_07_m02_004: It's called flamma. It grants humans a terrible power.
MID_SC13_07_m02_005: But I didn't expect him to be carrying any.\nWhen did he swipe that?
MID_SC13_07_m03: <TH>
MID_SC13_07_m03_001: Boss! Are you OK?!
MID_SC13_07_m03_002: His strength is unreal. Where did he attain\nsuch power?
MID_SC13_07_m04: <TH>
MID_SC13_07_m04_001: That is an unorthodox style. I doubt you are a\nmere priest.
MID_SC13_07_m04_002: Are you of the White Egg, like that Anatolia woman?
MID_SC13_07_m04_003: What?! No, I-I'm...
MID_SC13_07_m04_004: Hmhm. If you'd rather not admit it, I won't force\nthe issue.
MID_SC13_07_m05: <TH>
MID_SC13_07_m05_001: Rrragh! I've suffered worse from mosquitoes!
MID_SC13_07_m05_002: His tenacity is unbelievable...but I will finish him\nhere, I swear to it.
MID_SC13_07_m05_003: Hear me, Mahadu! Grant me the power of my\nancestors once more!
MID_SC13_07_m05_004: Hm?! This feeling...
MID_SC13_07_m05_005: My arm is surging with power. I am a match now\neven for this brute!
MID_SC13_07_e01: <TH>
MID_SC13_07_e01_001: Is he truly alone? Something about this makes\nme uneasy.
MID_SC13_07_e02: <TH>
MID_SC13_07_e02_001: Grr...
MID_SC13_07_e06: <TH>
MID_SC13_07_e06_001: Hrm?
MID_SC13_07_e07: <TH>
MID_SC13_07_e07_001: Your Majesty, I believe these risen dead are\nattempting to rally around Bahr Vahn.
MID_SC13_07_e07_002: I would not like to see the result if they are allowed\nto unite. Let us stop him before it happens.
MID_SC13_09_m01: <TH>
MID_SC13_09_m01_001: What's with this fog? I can't see two feet in front\nof my face!
MID_SC13_09_m01_002: It most likely rolled in from the nearby cliffs.
MID_SC13_09_m01_003: This is one of the reasons the Tritopater Corridor\nis a natural choke point.
MID_SC13_09_m01_004: They will be waiting inside the fog to ambush us.\nBe wary, Your Majesty.
MID_SC13_09_m02: <TH>
MID_SC13_09_m02_001: Your Majesty, please take care not to overextend\nyourself. It could have terrible consequences.
MID_SC13_09_m02_002: Your concern is appreciated but unnecessary.\nI am responsible for my own well-being.
MID_SC13_09_m02_003: Of course. Forgive me for speaking above my station.
MID_SC13_09_m03: <TH>
MID_SC13_09_m03_001: Strange that we should encounter the Har Hali here,\nof all places.
MID_SC13_09_m03_002: It is weird, right? I thought their home turf was\na ways away.
MID_SC13_09_m04: <TH>
MID_SC13_09_m04_001: No matter who trespasses on our land, we will\nshow no mercy.
MID_SC13_09_m05: <TH>
MID_SC13_09_m05_001: Ugh... I recognize that faint, acrid tang. They've\n{SetColor=Gold}dispersed poison{SetColor=Default} into the fog!
MID_SC13_09_m05_002: A {SetColor=Gold}prolonged battle is one we will lose{SetColor=Default}. Let us hurry\nto defeat this Nuzzuo!
MID_SC13_09_e17: <TH>
MID_SC13_09_e17_001: The poison... I can't...take any more...
MID_SC13_09_e01: <TH>
MID_SC13_09_e01_001: Your Majesty, we are fortunate that there are already\n{SetColor=Gold}devices to disperse the fog{SetColor=Default} established here.
MID_SC13_09_e02: <TH>
MID_SC13_09_e02_001: Including that one, there are {SetColor=Gold}three devices{SetColor=Default}, all told.\nI suggest incorporating them into our strategy.
MID_SC13_10_m01: <TH>
MID_SC13_10_m01_001: I've never seen this type of Demonic Beast before.\nThey're not the usual sandworms we get here.
MID_SC13_10_m01_002: Then our enemy is unknown to you as well?
MID_SC13_10_m01_003: Your Majesty, we may be able to learn their\nbehavioral patterns by observing them closely.
MID_SC13_10_m02: <TH>
MID_SC13_10_m02_001: Are you alright, Your Majesty?!
MID_SC13_10_m02_002: I am fine.
MID_SC13_10_m02_003: In truth, I normally loathe insects.
MID_SC13_10_m02_004: Yet oddly enough, I find I mind them less when\nthey are large enough to pose a challenge.
MID_SC13_10_m02_005: Guess you really do learn something new every day.
MID_SC13_10_m03: <TH>
MID_SC13_10_m03_001: I love eatin' bugs, but not when they're tryin' to\neat me back.
MID_SC13_10_m04: <TH>
MID_SC13_10_m04_001: Is this some sort of insect? It fits the bill well enough.
MID_SC13_10_m05: <TH>
MID_SC13_10_m05_001: It is time you surrendered the contents of your belly.
MID_SC13_10_m06: <TH>
MID_SC13_10_m06_001: Good. We have what we came for. There is no need\nfor us to linger.
MID_SC13_10_e01: <TH>
MID_SC13_10_e01_001: I note that some of them {SetColor=Gold}seem distinctive {SetColor=Default}from the\nrest. How peculiar...
MID_SC13_10_e01_002: And of what use is this observation? {SetColor=Gold}Strike quickly{SetColor=Default},\nif only to gain the information we need!
MID_SC13_10_e02: <TH>
MID_SC13_10_e02_001: There is no way to know which has the {SetColor=Gold}epimenium{SetColor=Default}.\n{SetColor=Gold}Keep defeating them until we find it!{SetColor=Default}
MID_SC13_10_e03: <TH>
MID_SC13_10_e03_001: Gah! These creatures are resilient. I fear a\nbrute-force approach will only exhaust us.
MID_SC13_10_e04: <TH>
MID_SC13_10_e04_001: There must be a more clever solution here. Perhaps\nthere is something to those {SetColor=Gold}distinctive-looking ones{SetColor=Default}...
MID_SC13_10_e05: <TH>
MID_SC13_10_e05_001: What?! What just happened?
MID_SC13_10_e05_002: Very interesting! When that one {SetColor=Gold}was attacked{SetColor=Default}, the\n{SetColor=Gold}impact rippled across its surroundings{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC13_10_e05_003: I do believe we may take advantage of this property\nto {SetColor=Gold}finish them all at once{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC13_10_e06: <TH>
MID_SC13_10_e06_001: What?! What just happened?
MID_SC13_10_e06_002: Very interesting! When that one {SetColor=Gold}was attacked{SetColor=Default}, the\n{SetColor=Gold}impact rippled across its surroundings{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC13_10_e06_003: If we attack one of these where they've gathered\ntogether, we may {SetColor=Gold}finish them all at once{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC13_11_m01: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_m01_001: To arms! We offer our souls and dedicate this fight\nto Yu Phas!
MID_SC13_11_m01_002: Huh. Yu Phas, eh?
MID_SC13_11_m02: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_m02_001: You're something else, you know that?
MID_SC13_11_m02_002: As are you, if the rumors of you carrying the blood\nof Dagda the Great are true.
MID_SC13_11_m02_003: Your pedigree is such that I shouldn't be surprised to\nfind you king of some nation or other.
MID_SC13_11_m06: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_m02_004: I appreciate the compliment, but that sort of thing\njust isn't me.
MID_SC13_11_m02_005: Doesn't seem like you either. Being queen must be\nstifling... Why keep at it?
MID_SC13_11_m02_006: Is it not clear? For the future of those who believe\nin me. For the sake of the faith we share.
MID_SC13_11_m02_007: To repay the debt of the great love shown to my\npeople in the past.
MID_SC13_11_m02_008: Hah! Always so serious! At this rate, we'll never see\neye to eye.
MID_SC13_11_m03: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_m03_001: Hey, are you really the richest guy in all of Dagda?
MID_SC13_11_m03_002: The legends are true. And the only one who has any\nchance of besting me is the Divine Sovereign himself.
MID_SC13_11_m03_003: Really? See, you say that, but I don't believe it\none bit.
MID_SC13_11_m03_004: Look me in the eyes. Is this the face of someone who\nwould lie to you?
MID_SC13_11_m03_005: Isn't that exactly the kind of cliché liars use to\nconvince people?
MID_SC13_11_m04: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_m04_001: I'll be going all in. I have grand ambitions of my own\nthat I plan on seeing fulfilled.
MID_SC13_11_m05: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_m05_001: Owowow... You got me... I'll be feeling that last one.
MID_SC13_11_m05_002: Still, that was fun. I'm impressed you got the\nbetter of me.
MID_SC13_11_e01: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e01_001: The Heroic Games are the ultimate test of martial\nprowess. But today's match is also a test of speed.
MID_SC13_11_e02: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e02_001: See those {SetColor=Gold}magic orbs{SetColor=Default} scattered on the battlefield?\nThe {SetColor=Gold}clan that collects the most will win{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC13_11_e02_002: The {SetColor=Gold}match will end{SetColor=Default} after {SetColor=Gold}12 rounds{SetColor=Default}. Collect as many\norbs as you can before time's up!
MID_SC13_11_e02_003: If both sides have the same number of orbs, we'll go\ninto overtime until a winner is declared!
MID_SC13_11_e36: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e36_001: {SetColor=Gold}Magic orbs{SetColor=Default}—they're the key to {SetColor=Gold}winning this match{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC13_11_e36_002: The {SetColor=Gold}match will end{SetColor=Default} after {SetColor=Gold}12 turns{SetColor=Default}. To win, you have\nto make sure your side has more when time's up!
MID_SC13_11_e36_003: If no one has any orbs, we'll go into overtime\nuntil a winner is declared!
MID_SC13_11_e05: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e05_001: Don't get complacent, now. If you are {SetColor=Gold}defeated{SetColor=Default},\nthe enemy will {SetColor=Gold}steal the orb{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC13_11_e05_002: Moreover, the orb's magic will {SetColor=Gold}lower defenses{SetColor=Default},\nso, allies, keep those orb bearers safe!
MID_SC13_11_e08: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e08_001: Now then, {SetColor=Gold}each person can hold only one orb{SetColor=Default}.\nNo doubling up, now!
MID_SC13_11_e06: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e06_001: {SetColor=Gold}Those who are defeated{SetColor=Default} will {SetColor=Gold}return to their clan's\nbase{SetColor=Default}. There's no exiting this stage.
MID_SC13_11_e09: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e09_001: Everyone understand? Then let's begin! Great\nwarriors... Commence the match!
MID_SC13_11_e11: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e11_001: This battle is a fierce back and forth! Which clan will\nseize the glory?
MID_SC13_11_e13: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e13_001: Look at that! An orb's been claimed—and it's\nlowered their defenses. Can they hold on to it?
MID_SC13_11_e14: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e14_001: <DLG>Cannot hold more than one orb.
MID_SC13_11_e19: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e19_001: Here are the final tallies. Tale of the Moon, led by\nTalimun, picked up {Variable=6}!
MID_SC13_11_e19_002: And as for Megaira's Beacon, led by Theodora...\nthe number is {Variable=5}!
MID_SC13_11_e28: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e28_001: Thus concludes the match! Now, let us move on to\nthe results.
MID_SC13_11_e29: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e29_001: The final tally is... Well, I'll be! It's a tie! With that,\nwe will enter overtime!
MID_SC13_11_e29_002: Strategy is of the essence—to grab a new orb, or steal\na foe's? As soon as the tie breaks, the match ends!
MID_SC13_11_e29_003: The moment there's one orb's difference between\nthe clans, the winner is decided. Now, begin!
MID_SC13_11_e31: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e31_001: The winner of this battle is...
MID_SC13_11_e32: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e32_001: Megaira's Beacon!
MID_SC13_11_e33: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e33_001: Hm. I rather enjoyed that.
MID_SC13_11_e34: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e34_001: Tale of the Moooon!
MID_SC13_11_e35: <TH>
MID_SC13_11_e35_001: Whew! Rough luck, Majesty. I'm sure you'll get 'em\nnext time, and all that. Now, about our deal...
MID_SC13_11_e35_002: How agonizing to have come so far and fallen short...
MID_SC13_12_m01: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_m01_001: When we first met, I thought you to be little more\nthan a minor obstacle.
MID_SC13_12_m01_002: The time has come for me to defeat you and end\nour ill-fated entanglement.
MID_SC13_12_m02: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_m02_001: No! It can't be...
MID_SC13_12_m02_002: Has the warding chain I just received from Zenon\nalready begun to fail?
MID_SC13_12_m02_003: This is absurd! I should have much more time than\nthis. What is happening?
MID_SC13_12_m02_004: Could the arm itself have gained in strength\nover time?
MID_SC13_12_m03: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_m03_001: I know you already know this, but I'm not planning\non losing this fight.
MID_SC13_12_m03_002: You stand before me undaunted? I see that the boy\nhas come into his own.
MID_SC13_12_m04: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_m04_001: The boy has grown strong. His skill has reached\nnew heights.
MID_SC13_12_m04_002: There is more to this than that new spear of his.\nI doubt this is coincidence.
MID_SC13_12_m04_003: How could he have attained such power in so short\na time?
MID_SC13_12_m05: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_m05_001: Unleash my power... Destroy everything.
MID_SC13_12_m05_002: There it is...that voice again. It's progressing too fast.
MID_SC13_12_m10: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_m05_003: Theodora? You're acting kind of weird.
MID_SC13_12_m11: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_m05_004: How can this boy Cai be so unaffected by the power\nconsuming me?
MID_SC13_12_m05_005: The demon god's abnormal strength wreaks havoc on\nthe mind. Is he suppressing it somehow?
MID_SC13_12_m05_006: And if so...does this mean my own weakness is\nto blame?
MID_SC13_12_m05_007: Ah! What is this feeling?
MID_SC13_12_m06: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_m06_001: Let us start this match afresh. I shall enjoy sparring\nwith you, Cai!
MID_SC13_12_m08: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_m06_002: Great! I'm gonna give it all I got, Theodora!
MID_SC13_12_m07: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_m07_001: Wow, Theodora... You're tough.
MID_SC13_12_m07_002: Haha... Guess I lose.
MID_SC13_12_m07_003: Cai...
MID_SC13_12_m09: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_m07_004: After a fierce battle, the last one standing is\nQueen Theodora!
MID_SC13_12_m07_005: Everyone, give these fearsome warriors the biggest\nround of applause!
MID_SC13_12_e01: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_e01_001: I see they are employing magical {SetColor=Gold}barriers{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC13_12_e01_002: There are {SetColor=Gold}two devices{SetColor=Default} within reach. They may be the\nkey to {SetColor=Gold}dispelling these barriers{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC13_12_e05: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_e05_001: Hm? Nothing happened.
MID_SC13_12_e06: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_e06_001: Does lowering the barrier require activating\n{SetColor=Gold}both devices{SetColor=Default}?
MID_SC13_12_e08: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_e08_001: The switch reset. I see now that we must {SetColor=Gold}activate\nboth switches within a single turn{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC13_12_e10: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_e10_001: The first barrier is no more! Let us press our advance\nthat we might eliminate the second one as well.
MID_SC13_12_e13: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_e13_001: That troublesome barrier is no more. Come, let us\nsettle this matter with the boy.
MID_SC13_12_e14: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_e14_001: You made it past the barrier, but you're not allowed\nto go any farther!
MID_SC13_12_e15: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_e15_001: I'm not scared of you guys! W-we're going to win!
MID_SC13_12_e16: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_e16_001: Hm. They will do what they can to keep us from\nour target.
MID_SC13_12_e17: <TH>
MID_SC13_12_e17_001: Theodora's forces are strong, but I've got your back!
MID_SC13_13_m01: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_m01_001: So you've finally come in person, my dear sister!\nHow gracious of you to take me up on my invitation.
MID_SC13_13_m01_002: Behold! I will kill you here and return triumphant\nas the king of Saramis!
MID_SC13_13_m01_003: I see that you still cling to your foolishness.
MID_SC13_13_m01_004: You have always lusted for power. It has been your\ngreatest weakness from the start.
MID_SC13_13_m01_005: A sovereign's power is to be used for the people.\nYour failure to understand that is your downfall.
MID_SC13_13_m01_006: How dare you lecture me as if you were superior!
MID_SC13_13_m01_007: Power without principles makes for a worthless\nmonarch.
MID_SC13_13_m01_008: "Principles"? They will make pretty dust on your\ngrave after I crush them to bits!
MID_SC13_13_m02: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_m02_001: I must say I had hoped for better from Prince Dyan.
MID_SC13_13_m02_002: Surely he had time to reflect inward while on that\nremote island.
MID_SC13_13_m02_003: But alas, he seems not to have grown at all since\nour last encounter.
MID_SC13_13_m02_004: Enough dancing around it, Bonaventure. Simply say\nthat my decision put off the inevitable.
MID_SC13_13_m02_005: Your words, my queen, not mine.
MID_SC13_13_m02_006: Argh...
MID_SC13_13_m03: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_m03_001: Theodora. We've come to pay the debt we owe you\nfor borrowing your ship.
MID_SC13_13_m03_002: Soldiers of Kunlun stand ready at your side.
MID_SC13_13_m03_003: A most unexpected ally. I am grateful, Anatolia.
MID_SC13_13_m03_004: We shall make good use of your assistance. Let us\njoin forces and rout them together!
MID_SC13_13_m10: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_m03_005: It is greatly heartening to see them come to our aid.
MID_SC13_13_m03_006: Indeed. A good reminder that it never hurts to have\nfavors to call in.
MID_SC13_13_m04: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_m04_001: You cannot defeat me, Dyan.
MID_SC13_13_m04_002: Oh, no? I'll see you in tears soon enough,\nmy dear sister!
MID_SC13_13_m05: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_m05_001: Um...hey, Prince Dyan...
MID_SC13_13_m05_002: Well, well, if it isn't Tabatha's daughter! Curse you\nfor shrugging off the debt your house owes me.
MID_SC13_13_m05_003: Traitor! For that I should lop your head from your\nshoulders where you stand!
MID_SC13_13_m05_004: All this is doing is making me feel bad that my dad\never believed in you.
MID_SC13_13_m06: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_m06_001: I will show you firsthand that it is not merely guile\nthat makes King Dyan so dangerous!
MID_SC13_13_m07: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_m07_001: Damn you, northern barbarians! See how you fare\nagainst a true Mosa warrior!
MID_SC13_13_m08: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_m08_001: All of you, lay down your arms and surrender! I have\ntaken your leader, Dyan, as my captive.
MID_SC13_13_m08_002: Know that any further fighting is pointless,\nand accept your defeat with grace!
MID_SC13_13_e06: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_e06_001: Our artillerists are in position, Your Majesty.\nGive the order whenever you wish!
MID_SC13_13_e06_004: Consider it given! Rain death upon all those who ally\nthemselves with Dyan!
MID_SC13_13_e13: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_e13_001: Anatolia's group is outside the walls, but I believe we\ncan let them into the fortress using the {SetColor=Gold}warp tiles{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC13_13_e13_002: {SetColor=Gold}Activating that switch {SetColor=Default}will make the {SetColor=Gold}warp tiles{SetColor=Default}\nready for our use.
MID_SC13_13_e17: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_e17_001: There it is! We can {SetColor=Gold}warp{SetColor=Default} into the fortress from that\nspot. Let's hurry to Theodora's side!
MID_SC13_13_e18: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_e18_001: Are the enemy reinforcements spent? Well done.\nArtillerists, you may fall back.
MID_SC13_13_e18_002: Yes, Your Majesty! May fortune favor you in the rest\nof the battle!
MID_SC13_13_e19: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_e19_001: Klapka, I want my dear sister dead. Do you hear\nme?! All the credit can be yours, if you wish!
MID_SC13_13_e19_002: This man... Send out the hidden reserves! We halt\ntheir advance here!
MID_SC13_13_e24: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_e24_001: The gate is open. The finale is near at hand. Do not\nallow yourselves carelessness now!
MID_SC13_13_e25: <TH>
MID_SC13_13_e25_001: Hm? Those {SetColor=Gold}censers{SetColor=Default}... If we {SetColor=Gold}break them{SetColor=Default}, their ashes\nwill scatter and {SetColor=Gold}hamper{SetColor=Default} our foes.
MID_SC13_13_e25_002: Though we would not be immune. Better then to\n{SetColor=Gold}break them from afar{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC13_XX_Rewind_e01: <TH>
MID_SC13_XX_Rewind_e01_001: What is this? The bag of sand that strange figure\ngave me is glowing.